index 48b9049..cb78f29 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,7 +6,23 @@ A small team notes app. Next.js App Router + TypeScript + Tailwind.
 
 - Users live in `src/lib/users.ts` as an in-memory list.
 - `/dashboard` shows the current user and the team.
-- There is no sign-in, no billing, and no email yet.
+- Auth is Auth.js (NextAuth v5, `src/auth.ts`): Google, email/password, and
+  magic-link email (via Resend) all resolve to the same user record through a
+  custom adapter (`src/lib/auth-adapter.ts`) backed by `src/lib/users.ts`.
+  Sessions are JWT-based; see the `jwt` callback for how "sign out of all
+  devices" invalidates them.
+- `/account` (`src/app/account/`) lets a signed-in user change or set their
+  password, sign out of every device, and delete their account.
+- There is no billing yet.
+
+### Why not Clerk?
+
+`docs/clerk.md` documents Clerk as an option, but this app stayed on Auth.js:
+requirements were magic links + a password/session/delete-account page — all
+things Auth.js does natively — and adding a hosted identity service would mean
+new vendor lock-in and a paid dependency for functionality already covered.
+Auth.js also kept the existing in-memory user store and Google/credentials
+setup intact instead of a rewrite.
 
 ## Develop
 
